  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 231 PM CDT Sun Aug 30 2026\n\nWarm and dry conditions are expected across the majority of South \nTexas this week, with the exception being the Victoria Crossroads. \nAs the tropical disturbance across the northern Gulf continues \nmoving west-northwest ward, warm moist air will advect into the \nregion. This will promote heat index values of 109-111 degrees and \nmoderate to extreme levels of heat risk. If the tropical disturbance \nwas to get better organize and strengthen (currently 50% chance for \nthe next 48 hours), it can become a short-lived tropical depression \nor tropical storm. As of this moment, no direct impacts are \nanticipated except for medium (40-60%) chances for showers and \nthunderstorms across the Victoria Crossroads. \n\nMore heat safety information can be found at weather.gov/heat",
